  "dom_id": "step-q2111",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "$-2+4=$",
  "worked_solution": "**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $4$ to $-2,$ we start at $-2$ on a number line and move $4$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14149949/assets/291bb445c414ae60c0093038554a780370b3e4d747e7e51a737aa15ffa7a6cf0.png)\n\nWe end up at $2.$ So, $-2+4=2.$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-2+4=4-2=2\n$$",
